staff my name is Stephanie Lowe I live at 5421 Hamilton Avenue Cheyenne Wyoming 82009 and I'm a preservation specialist in the community I have a master's degree in historic preservation from Boston architectural college and I'm here tonight to support the passing of this ordinance first and foremost I applaud the planning and development office for putting forward an incentive for historic preservation we don't have much of this in this city or state for that matter so any small opportunity is always a win secondly I'd like to remind everyone that this is an optional incentive program historic property owners are not required to participate if Property Owners do decide to participate from my understanding of the ordinance proposed there are only a few things that could actually be considered restrictive under this permit review for all

historic districts it's only the exterior of a building that needs to be maintained to consider its historic Integrity this would include windows and doors citing and any additions and removals to the structure for all interior changes they are not regulated to maintain the contributing value of the property so for those private property owners their kitchen or bathroom remodel should not necessarily be included in the review but is still allowed under this permit fee waiver program also of note the program is only for contributing historic structures in historic districts of which there is only seven more Haven Heights the Dubois block capital north and capital north expansion Lakeview Rainsford south side and the downtown and expanded downtown districts there are other properties that are not part of a district but that are still listed on the national register of historic places like the capitol the airport building terminal the old one the Federal Building several churches and

the atlas theater to name a few there are also the multiple Cheyenne historic schools and the warehouse multiple property nomination form there were some concern on how Property Owners know if they live in a contributing structure or not and I'd like to briefly speak to this all properties have a record filed on the property located at the County recording office this should be pulled and shared with potential property buyers by the realtor this is maybe not always being done though when any changes are made to a historic district the current property owner must be notified and typically have to agree to being added to the National register if someone is looking to own an older property is there not any personal responsibility for checking to see if it is contributing or not a person typically does not just accidentally own a contributing structure without being at the very least interested in the historic property there was a suggestion that the Cheyenne historic preservation board should do more Outreach to current property owners but I think it would be easier to Target the Realtors and

educate them on what is required however the planning office has a brochure for historic property owners that could easily be made available or share with them this was created not quite 10 years ago by the historic preservation board and is available in the city's website there have been extensive and multiple studies done looking at property values of historic buildings and districts time and again it's been proven that historic districts help maintain if not increased property values consistently over time typically historic Property Owners take better care of their property and are more invested in them thereby stabilizing neighborhoods which benefits everybody if you are against a historic preservation portion of this ordinance I encourage you to only strike that portion and

approve the support for affordable housing and Downtown Development which are both greatly needed in this community lastly I'd like to leave you with this quote from The National Trust for historic preservation historic districts are a tangible linked to the Past in a way to bring meaning to history and people's lives they preserve the original character of buildings and streets while welcoming growth and Innovation within those spaces they are living active record of communities and their residents I encourage you to vote Yes tonight thank you thank you Stephanie is there anybody else in the audience want to speak to this ordinance before us you're just going to say ditto uh mayor Collins members of the council Dan Dorsch um

